 "notes": [
  "Separate track: it does not change the ImageJevBench core Capability Score or ranking.",
  "Public set only in this preview; the 546 sealed items (after quality control) are held back for official runs.",
  "Open-weight models via OpenRouter are measured end to end through the provider; latency includes the provider.",
  "Self-hosted models: one request at a time on one RTX PRO 6000 class GPU; cost = GPU seconds x $1.19/GPU-hour.",
  "Chat models state their own confidence in the answer JSON; Jev returns a native confidence.",
  "Moondream 3 and Florence-2 return a box but no confidence, so their Calibration is 0 by the track rule and their Box Capability is low; their Box Intelligence (pure box quality) is shown separately. On Box Intelligence, Moondream 3 is level with the best sub-second systems (71.4, against 70.2 for H2O Lightning 4B; the difference is within noise).",
  "Claude Haiku 5.5 and GPT-6 Luna were run with reasoning off at temperature 0; both are not fully deterministic at temperature 0. One GPT-6 Luna answer failed with a provider error and Moondream 3 returned no box for 6 items; these count as invalid.",
  "Moondream 3 (preview) is released under the Business Source License 1.1; we ran it only to measure it and do not offer it as a service.",
  "Molmo 2 (Ai2) answers with points, not boxes, so it cannot be scored on IoU and is not ranked; its point-in-box rate is shown below the table as a side metric.",
  "H2O Lightning 4B v1.4.1 states a confidence on only 16 % of its answers (v1.1: 94 %); a missing confidence counts as no confidence, so its Calibration is low and its Box Capability falls below v1.1 although its boxes are better (Box Intelligence 76.5 against 70.2, documents 53 against 26)."
 ],
